// @exec: {"yield_time_ms": 120000, "max_output_tokens": 1000}
const p=tools.image_gen__imagegen({prompt:"Use case: photorealistic-natural. Asset type: final-quality full-screen background for Japanese mystery escape game KISEN, landscape 16:9, 1536x864 or higher. A single cohesive ultra-photorealistic photograph inside an empty older Japanese local train at midnight, camera at standing passenger eye level looking diagonally towards the SIDE exit, not straight down a symmetrical aisle. Real stainless steel frames, faded desaturated teal vinyl bench on left foreground, worn pale grey floor, gentle cool fluorescent practical lighting, slightly warm spill from station outside. Mid right: fully open sliding side door, concrete platform visible outside. Back left: broad rain-speckled train window framing a deserted platform, rectangular weathered station sign reading exactly 'きさらぎ'. On left bench: a small brown canvas satchel with cream triangular baggage tag and two repaired stitches. Above the bench is a metal luggage rack with a small rectangular shallow metal equipment box and two overlapping sliding brass catches. No readable tiny marks on the catches; they will be shown in a dedicated close-up. One small used cream railway ticket lies visibly on the empty floor near the bench. Far right fixed wall holds a shallow weathered brass route case 25x35cm with blank dark face, five small horizontal circular dial sockets, and a tiny keyhole, clearly an installed train fitting. Camera locations and furniture must feel coherent, the door is reachable with no barricades. The atmosphere is quietly unsettling through absence and wet reflections, NOT ruined, gore, ghosts or exaggerated fog. Strong photograph realism, natural modest wear, coherent contact shadows, physically plausible perspective, no CGI look, no illustration, no game UI, no caption, no floating labels, no vignette hiding interactive things. Keep near objects and background legible, not extreme bokeh. Do not create a collage or split panel.",transparent_background:false});
await yield_control();
const r=await p; store("train_gen",r); if(r&&typeof r==="object")text(Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(r).filter(([k])=>!["image_url","data"].includes(k)))); else text(r);

