["store",{referenced_image_paths:[base+"exec-9f059b78-c96a-4f1d-b102-612ebf38dd9d.png"],prompt:"Use case: photorealistic-natural. Same KISEN rural station, a low parcel corridor and small storeroom beneath old beams. Landscape16:9 eye-level photograph, dim but legible practical light, warm grey walls and old wood, cool damp floor. A large CLOSED wooden railway parcel chest centered at x38% y61%, old iron bands, flat small rectangular brass four-wheel lock face without readable digits. Six cream paper waybills clipped to a wooden board ABOVE the chest, arranged2x3, no readable tiny text, clearly paper tags. A few other stacked wood parcels on left, no treasure chests or fantasy locks. Passage exits BACK LEFT towards station office. Far RIGHT the passage splits into a visible closed little wooden door toward lamp hut at x76% y42% (a small four-digit lock, unreadable at this distance) and a narrow open outdoor side door at x93% y45% showing wet path and dark trees towards tunnel. Coherent architecture: separate doors, no impossible wall openings. Small old wheeled cart parked to side so center passage is now walkable. No people, no high-tech screens, no UI, no collage. Photoreal night location.",transparent_background:false}]
